                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2d166f0d-bf14-476d-8a23-b0606e8c571b",
                        "entry_id": "748fce39-f2b5-3e08-9229-35070ffe3747",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "noumènes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3215e5c6-f19d-36dd-9169-53e5ffe09ee7",
                        "entry_id": "748fce39-f2b5-3e08-9229-35070ffe3747",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chez Kant, désigne la chose en soi, par opposition à phénomène, qui désigne l’objet tel qu’il nous apparaît en passant par notre esprit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3284038f-f544-4d68-b3e6-a7dd79a9396d",
                                "sense_id": "3215e5c6-f19d-36dd-9169-53e5ffe09ee7",
                                "text": "Donc, il n’est tel noumène qu’à condition d’être déjà engagé dans le phénomène; il n’est telle liberté, tel moi libre, qu’à la condition d’être enveloppé de nécessités."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "593356aa-a385-4586-a23c-b8252cb7103b",
                        "source_entry_id": "748fce39-f2b5-3e08-9229-35070ffe3747",
                        "source_sense_id": "3215e5c6-f19d-36dd-9169-53e5ffe09ee7",
                        "target_lang_word": "noumenon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "noumenon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d1d5e57-e196-36f8-99c8-ce123baef0e1",
                                        "entry_id": "6e9db17e-d9be-388e-8d2d-ad63bff77472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A thing as it is independent of any conceptualization or perception by the human mind, postulated by practical reason but existing in a condition which is in principle unknowable and unexperienceable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "from Kantian philosophy on"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf5688ad-fbab-43a8-b9b5-2b272eed0ccc",
                                                "sense_id": "9d1d5e57-e196-36f8-99c8-ce123baef0e1",
                                                "text": "The final result of Kant's philosophy, expressed in the concisest terms, was the proposition, so humiliating to human cognition, but, at the same time, so fertile in consequences, that we can know only phenomena, or the outward appearances of things, but not the noumenon, or the thing in itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b10b0f65-5a95-4c2d-bafe-4e8ce1c93b57",
                                                "sense_id": "9d1d5e57-e196-36f8-99c8-ce123baef0e1",
                                                "text": "We have no specific concept of the noumenon, but think of it merely as whatever the object may be apart from the manner in which our knowledge exhibits it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1406399-2e91-429e-8e2e-c23c1dd0e2ed",
                                                "sense_id": "9d1d5e57-e196-36f8-99c8-ce123baef0e1",
                                                "text": "That, we have seen, is what prevents the two truths from collapsing into an appearance/reality or phenomenon/noumenon distinction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f7fa30d9-1de7-4a0c-a376-c46e29221b89",
                        "source_entry_id": "748fce39-f2b5-3e08-9229-35070ffe3747",
                        "source_sense_id": "3215e5c6-f19d-36dd-9169-53e5ffe09ee7",
                        "target_lang_word": "noúmeno",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "noúmeno",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04b2f7db-9c43-31f9-8b70-40ffb71a9c16",
                                        "entry_id": "17333a23-a692-3671-92d4-ad399801b2f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En la ontología de Immanuel Kant (1724-1804) y de sus discípulos, una cosa en la medida en que es independiente de cualquier conceptualización o percepción por la mente humana; una cosa en sí, postulada por razones prácticas pero existente en una situación que en principio no es conocible y no es experimentable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
